<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second War of Scottish Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1332">1332</a>–<a href="/years/1357">1357</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second War of Scottish Independence began in 1332 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-balliol">Edward Balliol</a>, backed by the 'Disinherited' nobles and later by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a>, invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> against the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> II. The Scots suffered heavy defeats at Dupplin Moor, Halidon Hill and Neville's Cross, where David was captured, but kept their independence. The war ended with the Treaty of Berwick of 1357, which released David for a ransom.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Second War of Independence</b> brought defeats at Halidon Hill in 1333 and Neville’s Cross in 1346, where David II was captured.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>It was the first major battle of the <b>Second War of Scottish Independence</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-11">11 August in history</a></li></ul></section>
